import ContentPage from "@/layouts/ContentPage.astro";
---
<ContentPage
  title="How We Verify Providers | SpedCentral"
  description="Every provider on SpedCentral goes through a credential and licensing review before their listing goes live. Here's exactly what that involves."
  heading="How We Verify Providers"
>
  <p>
    A directory is only useful if you can trust what's in it. Before any provider appears on SpedCentral, we go
    through the following review:
  </p>

  <h2>1. Credential &amp; licensing check</h2>
  <p>
    We confirm that any claimed license or certification (CCC-SLP, BCBA, OTR/L, state teaching or counseling
    licenses, etc.) is real and current, using the relevant state licensing board or certifying body's public
    lookup tool where one exists.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Business verification</h2>
  <p>
    For practices and companies, we confirm the business is actually operating at the address and under the name
    listed -- not just that a form was submitted.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Manual review before publishing</h2>
  <p>
    Every submission is reviewed by a person before it goes live. Nothing is published automatically the moment
    someone fills out a form. If something doesn't check out, we follow up with the provider before publishing, or
    we don't publish it at all.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Ongoing monitoring</h2>
  <p>
    Verification isn't one-and-done. We re-check listings periodically and act on user reports of outdated,
    inaccurate, or concerning information -- see <a href="/contact/">Contact Us</a> to report an issue with a
    specific listing.
  </p>

  <h2>What verification does <em>not</em> mean</h2>
  <p>
    Verification confirms that a provider's credentials and business are genuine. It is not a guarantee of the
    quality of care or service you'll receive, and it isn't a substitute for your own judgment -- read reviews, ask
    questions, and trust your instincts when choosing a provider for your family. SpedCentral is a directory, not
    an employer, referral agency, or medical/legal advisor, and providers listed here are independent businesses,
    not SpedCentral staff.
  </p>

  <h2>Sponsored listings are verified the same way</h2>
  <p>
    Paying for a featured/sponsored placement does not change or skip this review process. Every provider,
    sponsored or not, goes through the same credential check before appearing on SpedCentral.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
